Executive Summary 
(This is a one-page summary of the document, divided into the following subsections.)

Overview 

This document outlines the business requirements for developing a Google Apps Script automation designed to streamline the tracking of Shopify global actions, progress, and milestones. The proposed script will connect existing workflow tools (e.g., Google Sheets, Google Forms, or Google Workspace APIs) to automate status updates, generate progress notifications, and provide clear visibility into project timelines.

Background 

Currently, tracking action items, task completion, and progress against operational project milestones relies on manual data entry and recurring status meetings. This manual approach leads to several operational challenges:

Time Overhead: Team members spend significant effort manually updating status sheets and compiling report summaries.

Data Inconsistencies: Human error and delayed updates result in outdated or conflicting progress reporting.

Lack of Real-Time Visibility: Key stakeholders often lack instant insight into whether upcoming milestones are on track, delayed, or blocked.

To resolve these inefficiencies, a centralized, lightweight automation powered by Google Apps Script is required to standardize data capture and automate tracking workflows.

Objectives 

Automate Status Tracking: Reduce manual data entry by automatically recording action item status updates and calculating completion percentages against target milestones.

Improve Transparency: Provide real-time dashboards or automated notifications that alert stakeholders to upcoming or overdue milestones.

Increase Operational Efficiency: Cut time spent on manual progress reporting by at least [e.g., 50%].

Standardize Workflows: Establish a uniform method for task logging, ownership assignment, and milestone mapping across the organization.


Requirements Functional Requirements

Data Ingestion & Logging:

Automatically pull or append task entries from [e.g., a central Google Form or integrated Sheet].

Timestamp all updates and capture key attributes: Task ID, Action Item, Owner, Start Date, Target Milestone, Due Date, Status (Not Started / In Progress / Completed / Blocked), Notes and effectiveness score (validated / partially effective / no observable effect / insufficient evidence) 

Automated Calculations & Progress Tracking:

Dynamically calculate milestone completion rates (e.g., % of actions completed per milestone).

Flag items as "Overdue" or "At Risk" based on target dates, missed milestones, action effectiveness and status.

Automated Notifications & Alerts:

Send daily/weekly automated email summaries (via Gmail API) to action owners listing pending or overdue tasks.

Send instant notifications to project managers when a critical milestone status changes to "Blocked" or "Completed."

Reporting & Dashboarding:

Maintain a summary tab/dashboard within Google Sheets that reflects overall milestone progress and task breakdowns in real time.

Non-Functional Requirements

Execution Limit: Script execution times must run efficiently within standard Google Workspace quota limits.

Security & Permissions: Access restricted to authorized team members; script runs under appropriate service account or project permissions.

Maintainability: Code must be commented, modular, and easy to adjust if milestones or team structures change.


Target Audience 

POCs / Lead Administrators: Primary users who manage the underlying Google Sheets, monitor milestones, and review automated reports.

Action Item Owners / Team Members: Users responsible for completing tasks and providing updates via the standardized process.

Executive Stakeholders & Leadership: Consumers of high-level milestone progress summaries and dashboard updates.

Proposed Strategy Phase 

1: Architecture & Data Structure Design

Finalize the Google Sheets master tracking schema, defining clear columns for actions, dependencies, and milestones.

Phase 2: Apps Script Development

Develop custom Google Apps Script functions handling custom triggers (onEdit, time-driven triggers for periodic updates), dynamic status calculations, and automated email generation.

Phase 3: User Acceptance Testing (UAT)

Test the script using sample project data to verify trigger timing, notification formatting, and edge-case handling (e.g., blank fields, past due dates).

Phase 4: Deployment & Documentation

Deploy the finalized script, configure time-driven triggers, and train team members on standardized data entry guidelines.


